ontology biology
	version 1.0
	using imod, life
	in domain imod:Biology;

/**
 * ## Biological synthesis and membrane transfer
 *
 * Photosynthesis uses light in biological synthesis of energy-rich compounds.
 * Its meaning is not restricted to plants, oxygen production or one biochemical
 * pathway. MembraneTransport moves material across a biological membrane; the
 * transported substance, direction and mode of transfer distinguish particular
 * observations.
 *
 * A living individual and a portion of biological material have distinct
 * identities. Describing either process does not determine whether a cell or
 * organ is observed as an individual, a material structure or another kind of
 * entity. Models describe the participants, rates and conditions. Process names
 * alone do not establish a growth outcome or a newly instantiated organism.
 */
process Photosynthesis
    "Biological synthesis of energy-rich compounds using light energy.";

process MembraneTransport
    "Transfer of material across a biological membrane.";
